  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1150 AM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nHOT AND DRY CONDITIONS CONTINUE:\n\nHigh pressure remains to our south and with west through\nnorthwesterly flow, moisture will also stay to the south. What\nthis means for us is hot temperatures continue with the usual\nafternoon breezes. Highs will remain above normal for the\nforeseeable future though they will be slightly cooler today \nand tomorrow precluding any heat products. However, Friday \nonwards, temperatures increase and we will likely need some \nproducts then. As far as precip goes, might see a stray \nshower/storm over the weekend but with such dry sub-levels, do \nnot anticipate anything reaching the ground so the main concern \nwill be some gusty outflow winds and lightning. We might see \nsome changes next week as models are hinting at some moisture \nsneaking up underneath the high bringing more isolated to \nscattered showers and storms.",
